From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:33:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/ane: do not report the identify-only stop as a
 refusal

A platform marked identify_only (the T8132) stops after it has identified
its preload, by design, and says so:

  H16 preload identified; this SoC stops before power-up

That stop then goes through the same path as a real pre-RUN failure and
also logs an error:

  H16 stage program refused before RUN, error -95

Keep everything the stop does (the -EOPNOTSUPP, the refused state, the
release of power and mappings) and leave out only that error line for the
planned stop. Every other pre-RUN failure is still logged as before, and
with h16_power_unqualified set the power-up path is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
index 0b1ee65a8c..a89bab0f3e 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_backend.c
@@ -1651,6 +1651,7 @@ static int ane_h16_program_stage(struct ane_h16_device *h)
 static int ane_h16_advance(struct ane_h16_device *h, enum ane_h16_stage stage)
 {
 	enum ane_h16_stage target = stage > ANE_H16_STARTUP ? ANE_H16_STARTUP : stage;
+	bool planned_stop = false;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (h->refused || h->boot.failed || h->boot.quarantined)
@@ -1663,6 +1664,7 @@ static int ane_h16_advance(struct ane_h16_device *h, enum ane_h16_stage stage)
 		if (!ret && h->boot.soc->identify_only && !h16_power_unqualified) {
 			dev_info(h->dev, "H16 preload identified; this SoC stops before power-up\n");
 			ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+			planned_stop = true;
 		} else if (!ret && h->boot.soc->identify_only) {
 			dev_warn(h->dev, "H16 preload identified; unqualified power-up (h16_power_unqualified)%s\n",
 				 h->boot.soc->no_engine_tunables ? ", no engine tunables" : "");
@@ -1697,8 +1699,10 @@ static int ane_h16_advance(struct ane_h16_device *h, enum ane_h16_stage stage)
 		 h->boot.ran ? "; held until reboot" : "");
 	return 0;
 refuse:
-	dev_err(h->dev, "H16 stage %s refused before RUN, error %d\n",
-		ane_h16_stage_name(stage), ret);
+	/* The identify-only stop is the platform's design, not a failure. */
+	if (!planned_stop)
+		dev_err(h->dev, "H16 stage %s refused before RUN, error %d\n",
+			ane_h16_stage_name(stage), ret);
 	h->refused = true;
 	ane_h16_release(h);
 	return ret;
